{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Where are you.</b> He knew where he was. Rather, to enter into conversation with him — so that he would not be startled to answer if He punished him suddenly (Bereshit Rabbah). And likewise with Cain He said to him, ״אֵי הֶבֶל אָחִיךָ״ (Genesis 4), and likewise with Balaam, ״מִי הָאֲנָשִׁים הָאֵלֶּה עִמָּךְ״ (Numbers 22) — to enter into conversation with them. And likewise with Hezekiah, with the emissaries of Merodach-baladan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:22.253436296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}